   "en": "Lower bound: below it the skin would shrink inside muscle and bone — muscles do not thin with BMI, and the share of sampled deep-part vertices more than 2 mm outside the skin would exceed the default (0.1 %) by more than 1 percentage points; nor below 18.5, the lowest BMI of the fat-field table. Upper bound: 40, the highest BMI of the table."
